<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! carriage.disk.wins ~ a person settles one standoff toward the disk

`take-disk <uri> key=<key>` lands the file's words in the records for one standoff, riding the worn face's ingest leg. `keep-disk` lands the file's words WHOLE, with no merge, and lets the standoff's drafts go. A standoff first loads the file's side as drafts in the worn face's draft layer, and the collapse rules the person set in their daemon face (`$:/config/lares/shore/collapse/<rule>`) settle what they can; what stays raises one alert naming `keep-disk`, `keep-records`, and where drafts stand `keep-both` and `drafts`.

Where no base stands, `lares ingest` of the file names the same adoption. SETTLING STAYS A HAND ACT: the verb reads the hand behind this command first; an AI harness on its branch refuses `hand-act-only`, an unreadable branch `hand-unattested`, and `yes=true` approves nothing by itself. A terminal asks `Proceed? [y/N]` (the records give way to the file's present words); a JSON call off a terminal needs `yes=true`. The key comes from the alert; an answer that names a state that moved takes nothing.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/shows`>>

!! shows ~ take-the-disk

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`example` name=`take-the-disk` params=`uri/lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/example key/<key> ~ the file's words land in the records`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/takes`>>

!! takes ~ uri · key · bag · yes

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`arg` name=`uri` params=`takes/lar-address needs/required seat/1 as/<uri> ~ the carrier at the standoff`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`key` params=`takes/key needs/required ~ the standoff's key, as lares shore printed it`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`bag` params=`takes/bag-uri ~ the bag that holds the carrier`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`yes` params=`kind/switch ~ name the intent for a call off a terminal; approves nothing by itself`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/gate`>>

!! gate ~ hand-act

Testimony: the door checks; this slot grants nothing.

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`gate` name=`hand-act` params=`who/hand ~ a settling act reads the hand behind this command before anything else; an AI harness on its branch refuses hand-act-only, an unreadable branch hand-unattested, each naming the command the operator runs, and yes=true approves nothing by itself`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/refuses`>>

!! refuses ~ hand-act-only · hand-unattested · usage · a-state-that-moved

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`hand-act-only` params=`cure/[[carriage.disk.reads]] ~ an AI harness settles nothing; the line names the command the operator runs`>>
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`hand-unattested` params=`cure/[[carriage.disk.reads]] ~ the branch behind this command stays unreadable; read the shore, then run the act on your own terminal`>>
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`usage` params=`cure/[[carriage.disk.wins uri/<uri> key/<key>]] ~ a carrier and the standoff's key both stand required`>>
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`a-state-that-moved` params=`~ an answer names the state its giver read (a standoff's key, or the count that stands pending); where that state moved, the island refuses by name and nothing changes`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/answers`>>

!! answers ~ took · aborted

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`band` name=`took` params=`exit/0 ~ the file's side won; the line names the carrier and its bag`>>
<<has entity=`band` name=`aborted` params=`exit/1 ~ the person answered no at the prompt`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

